From 275cdab02c143543b39517618a2c9baaa2adf05d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:45:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rigid body modes given to the preconditioners of PETSc

When the number of components of the unknowns is the space dimension (2
or 3) and the unknowns are ordered by vector dimension, the matrices
converted for PETScLinearSolver and PETScPreconditioner receive the
number of components as block size and the rigid body modes of the finite
element space as near null space (MatNullSpaceCreateRigidBody, from the
coordinates of the nodes): the algebraic multigrid of PETSc (GAMG) then
aggregates the nodes and builds its coarse spaces from these modes. On the
beam of PETScSolversTest, the conjugate gradient needs 15 iterations
instead of 51. Option RigidBodyModes (true by default) to disable them.

The coordinates of the nodes of the true degrees of freedom are computed
by a shared internal function (NodesCoordinates.hxx), for the other
algebraic multigrids which need them.
